date overdue, or does it only become overdue from day 8?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Overdue from day 7 (today >= due date + 7)\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Does reminder history record only successful sends, or every attempt including failures?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Every attempt, each with a delivery status (sent / failed + reason)\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"Payments are out of scope, so how does an invoice leave the overdue list (for example, once it is paid)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A paid/closed status in the existing invoice data removes it automatically\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Can staff send another reminder for an invoice that was already reminded, and how do we stop accidental double clicks?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Repeat reminders allowed at any time; only accidental double submits are blocked\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-1,ASM-2,ASM-3,ASM-4,ASM-5 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Should 'overdue' be worked out each time from the due date and paid status, or saved as a status on the invoice record?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Worked out each time; nothing is written to invoices\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Where does the customer's email address come from, and what happens if there isn't one or there are several?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Single email field on the existing customer record; block sending if missing\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"What counts as a 'delivery failure' that gets recorded with a reason?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Send-time errors plus later bounces reported back by the provider\",\n  \"by\": \"ASM-6,ASM-7,ASM-8 (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Add an invoice reminders API endpoint that returns a list of overdue invoices to authenticated staff users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"An invoice is included in the overdue list only if it has open status, has a due date, and today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus a configurable overdue threshold, which defaults to 7 days.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Invoices with any status other than open, such as paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft or written off, are excluded from the overdue list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Invoices with no due date are excluded from the overdue list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"When an invoice's status changes away from open, it stops appearing in the overdue list on the next request without any other action.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Overdue status is calculated at query time and no overdue flag or status is written to invoice records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Each entry in the overdue list includes the invoice number, customer name, amount, due date, and days overdue.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Days overdue is calculated as the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list can be filtered by customer, returning only that customer's overdue invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list can be filtered by a days-overdue bucket of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90, or 91 and over, with bucket boundaries included.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Customer filter and days-overdue bucket filter can be combined in a single request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Requesting the overdue list with a bucket value outside the four allowed buckets returns a 400 response that names the allowed bucket values.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Requests to the overdue list endpoint without valid staff authentication are rejected with HTTP 401 and return no invoice or customer data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The overdue list endpoint must respond quickly at expected data sizes, with or without filters.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}